      <div id="articlesList">
        <!-- Article 1 -->
        <div class="card const-card" data-part="Part I" data-keys="1 article 1 name territory union bharat states" onclick="showArticleModal('Article 1: Name and territory of the Union', 'India, that is Bharat, shall be a Union of States. The territory includes States, UTs, and acquired territories.', 'State of West Bengal v. Union of India (1963)', 'Establishes an indestructible Union composed of destructible States (Parliament can alter boundaries under Art 3).')">
          <div class="card-meta"><span>Part I • Union & Territory</span><span>Tap Details ➔</span></div>
          <h4>Article 1 — Name and Territory of the Union</h4>
          <p data-en="India, that is Bharat, shall be a Union of States." data-ur="Hindustan, yani Bharat, riyasaton ka ek ittehad (Union of States) hoga.">India, that is Bharat, shall be a Union of States.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Article 13 -->
        <div class="card const-card" data-part="Part III" data-keys="13 judicial review fundamental rights inconsistency void" onclick="showArticleModal('Article 13: Laws inconsistent with Fundamental Rights', 'All laws in force in India inconsistent with Part III shall, to the extent of such inconsistency, be void.', 'Kesavananda Bharati (1973), State of Madras v. V.G. Row (1952)', 'The cornerstone of Judicial Review in India. Doctrines of Severability, Eclipse, and Waiver stem directly from Article 13.')">
          <div class="card-meta"><span>Part III • Fundamental Rights</span><span>Tap Details ➔</span></div>
          <h4>Article 13 — Laws Inconsistent with Part III</h4>
          <p data-en="Constitutional basis of judicial review: any law infringing fundamental rights is void to that extent." data-ur="Judicial review ki buniyad: Aaeeni buniyadi haqooq ke khilaf banne wala koi bhi qanoon us had tak baatil hoga.">Constitutional basis of judicial review: any law infringing fundamental rights is void to that extent.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Article 14 -->
        <div class="card const-card" data-part="Part III" data-keys="14 equality before law equal protection arbitrariness royappa" onclick="showArticleModal('Article 14: Equality before law', 'The State shall not deny to any person equality before the law or equal protection of the laws within the territory of India.', 'E.P. Royappa v. State of TN (1974), Maneka Gandhi v. UOI (1978)', 'Guarantees equality and outlaws arbitrariness in state action. Intelligible differentia test and reasonable nexus test apply.')">
          <div class="card-meta"><span>Part III • Fundamental Rights</span><span>Tap Details ➔</span></div>
          <h4>Article 14 — Equality Before Law</h4>
          <p data-en="Prohibits arbitrariness and ensures equal protection of the laws for all persons." data-ur="Har shakhs ke liye qanoon ke samne barabari aur yaksaan qanooni tahaffuz ki zamanat deta hai.">Prohibits arbitrariness and ensures equal protection of the laws for all persons.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Article 19 -->
        <div class="card const-card" data-part="Part III" data-keys="19 freedoms speech expression assembly trade anuradha bhasin" onclick="showArticleModal('Article 19: Protection of Six Freedoms', 'Guarantees freedoms of speech, assembly, association, movement, residence, and trade/occupation to citizens.', 'Shreya Singhal v. UOI (2015), Anuradha Bhasin v. UOI (2020)', 'Freedoms are not absolute; subject to reasonable restrictions under Clauses (2) through (6). Proportionality test applies.')">
          <div class="card-meta"><span>Part III • Fundamental Rights</span><span>Tap Details ➔</span></div>
          <h4>Article 19 — Protection of Core Freedoms</h4>
          <p data-en="Six fundamental democratic freedoms protected for citizens, governed by reasonable statutory restrictions." data-ur="Shehriyon ko 6 buniyadi aazadiyan faraham karta hai, jin par munasib qanooni pabandiyan lagayi ja sakti hain.">Six fundamental democratic freedoms protected for citizens, governed by reasonable statutory restrictions.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Article 21 -->
        <div class="card const-card" data-part="Part III" data-keys="21 life personal liberty privacy maneka gandhi puttaswamy" onclick="showArticleModal('Article 21: Protection of Life & Personal Liberty', 'No person shall be deprived of his life or personal liberty except according to procedure established by law.', 'Maneka Gandhi v. UOI (1978), K.S. Puttaswamy v. UOI (2017)', 'Expanded via judicial activism to encompass right to privacy, clean environment, free legal aid, speedy trial, and dignity.')">
          <div class="card-meta"><span>Part III • Fundamental Rights</span><span>Tap Details ➔</span></div>
          <h4>Article 21 — Protection of Life & Personal Liberty</h4>
          <p data-en="The bedrock of constitutional liberty. Encompasses right to live with human dignity and privacy." data-ur="Zindagi aur zaati aazadi ka buniyadi tahaffuz. Isme izzat ke sath jeene aur privacy ka haq shamil hai.">The bedrock of constitutional liberty. Encompasses right to live with human dignity and privacy.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Article 32 -->
        <div class="card const-card" data-part="Part III" data-keys="32 remedies supreme court writs habeas corpus ambedkar" onclick="showArticleModal('Article 32: Constitutional Remedies', 'Guarantees the right to move the Supreme Court directly for enforcement of Fundamental Rights by issuing Writs.', 'Fertilizer Corporation Kamgar Union (1981), Bandhua Mukti Morcha (1984)', 'Dr. B.R. Ambedkar termed it the Heart and Soul of the Constitution. Prerogative writs: Habeas Corpus, Mandamus, Prohibition, Quo Warranto, Certiorari.')">
          <div class="card-meta"><span>Part III • Remedies</span><span>Tap Details ➔</span></div>
          <h4>Article 32 — Remedies for Enforcement of Rights</h4>
          <p data-en="Prerogative writs enforceable directly before the Supreme Court for protecting Fundamental Rights." data-ur="Buniyadi haqooq ke tahaffuz ke liye seedha Supreme Court mein writ dakhil karne ka aaeeni haq.">Prerogative writs enforceable directly before the Supreme Court for protecting Fundamental Rights.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Article 368 -->
        <div class="card const-card" data-part="Part XX" data-keys="368 amendment constituent power basic structure kesavananda" onclick="showArticleModal('Article 368: Power of Parliament to Amend Constitution', 'Parliament may amend by way of addition, variation, or repeal any provision of the Constitution as per procedure.', 'Kesavananda Bharati v. State of Kerala (1973), Minerva Mills (1980)', 'Constituent power is not unlimited. Parliament cannot destroy or alter the Basic Structure of the Constitution.')">
          <div class="card-meta"><span>Part XX • Amendment</span><span>Tap Details ➔</span></div>
          <h4>Article 368 — Parliament's Power to Amend</h4>
          <p data-en="Constituent amending mechanism, bounded by the non-negotiable Basic Structure Doctrine." data-ur="Aaeen mein tarmeem karne ka parliamentary ikhtiyar, jo Basic Structure doctrine ke tehat paband hai.">Constituent amending mechanism, bounded by the non-negotiable Basic Structure Doctrine.</p>
